# BAS S-ClsBot / I-Case3: Constructor match arms with disjoint variant tags.
# [try [fn [] 42]] returns Variant(Ok, Int(42)). The I-Case3 rule in infer_match
# accumulates negations: after the [Ok v] arm, remaining_scrutinee gains ~"Ok"
# via Type::Negation. S-ClsBot: Intersection([scrutinee, "Ok"]) ∩ ~"Ok" = Never.
# The [Err _] arm correctly matches an uninhabited scrutinee type.
[result: [try [fn [] 42]]
 value: [match result
   [Ok v]  v
   [Err _] 0]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Variant(Ok, Int(42)), "value": Int(42)})
